+---
+id: task-003-long-stay-rental-discount-10-off-rentals-of-3-days-or-more
+type: task
+title: "Long-stay rental discount: 10% off rentals of 3 days or more"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Long-stay rental discount: 10% off rentals of 3 days or more
+
+The school wants to reward customers who stay longer.
+
+## Requested behaviour
+
+A rental of 3 days or more costs 10% less than its full price (`dailyPrice` times the number of days).
+Quotes and bookings both show the reduced total.
+
+## Interpretation
+
+- The threshold is inclusive: a period of exactly 3 days gets the discount; 1 or 2 days do not.
+- The discount is 10% of the full price. The total is in euro cents, so the discounted total is rounded to the
+  nearest cent, with ties rounded up (`Math.round`). Example: 3 days at 2 000 cents is 6 000 full, 5 400 discounted.
+- `quote` and `book` return the discounted total in `total`. The full price is not exposed.
+- `availability` is unchanged; it does not price anything.
+- Invalid periods and unknown items still throw, as before.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- A 1- or 2-day rental is priced at full price.
+- A 3-day rental and a longer one are priced at 90% of full price, rounded to the cent.
+- `quote` and `book` agree on the same discounted total.
+- Tests are deterministic and in-process, with no external services.
+- The README describes the discount.
